    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Description\n\nI have a mapping with a custom source name:\n```lua\nvim.keymap.set('n', '<Leader>pr', function()\n  MiniPick.builtin.grep_live(nil, { source = { name = 'Grep in VIMRUNTIME', cwd = vim.env.VIMRUNTIME } })\nend)\n```\nBut changing the pattern matching method (`C-e`) or adding a glob (`C-o`) overrides that name with the hardcoded `Grep live`:\nhttps://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/8d86a057fa14681cf7cab74ea7cba894a0abe14f/lua/mini/pick.lua#L1421\nIt would be great to preserve the user-provided source name when using `C-e` and `C-o` mappings.",
