        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Thanks for the fix! Since `get_name()` now includes the custom source name, I think it makes sense to show it with the tool/method right away instead of after using picker-specific actions (like the default picker does):\n\n```patch\ndiff --git a/lua/mini/pick.lua b/lua/mini/pick.lua\nindex 52ad8c0..26614ab 100644\n--- a/lua/mini/pick.lua\n+++ b/lua/mini/pick.lua\n@@ -1421,7 +1421,7 @@ MiniPick.builtin.grep_live = function(local_opts, opts)\n   local globs_suffix = #globs == 0 and '' or (' | ' .. table.concat(globs, ', '))\n   local init_name, method = opts.source.name or 'Grep live', local_opts.method\n   local get_name = function() return string.format('%s (%s %s%s)', init_name, tool, method, globs_suffix) end\n-  opts.source.name = opts.source.name or get_name()\n+  opts.source.name = get_name()\n\n   local cwd = H.full_path(opts.source.cwd or vim.fn.getcwd())\n   local set_items_opts, spawn_opts = { do_match = false, querytick = H.querytick }, { cwd = cwd }\n```",
            "created_at": "2026-08-26T08:42:33Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/2540#issuecomment-5422804195",
            "id": 5422804195,
